[00:00:26] Speaker1:
    When opening a service request, setting a severity level is a critical part of the process.

[00:00:33] Speaker2:
    This is what drives and sets the priority of your ticket moving forward.

[00:00:38] Speaker1:
    Severity 1 means it is absolutely critical to your business operations.

[00:00:43] Speaker2:
    Severity 3 and 4 are for more general configuration and troubleshooting cases.

[00:00:48] Speaker1:
    If you have a severity 1 or a severity 2 request, we strongly encourage that you called Cisco Support. For a severity three and four request, go to Support Case Manager to open and track your request.

[00:01:02] Speaker2:
    You can also reach support by using the worldwide contact numbers or by connecting with Cisco Support Assistant. To expedite the resolution on your service request, you will need a valid Cisco.com user ID, an active support contract number, a serial number for the product you're opening the case on, and finally a clear and accurate problem description along with the symptoms.

